.TH MYGREP 3 "September 2026" "libmyutils 0.4.1" "libmyutils Manual"
.SH NAME
mygrep \- find lines in a file that contain a string
.SH SYNOPSIS
#include "myfilefunctions.h"
.PP
.B int mygrep(FILE *fp, const char *search_str, char ***matches);
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mygrep()
reads
.I fp
line by line and saves a copy of every line that contains
.IR search_str .
The lines are returned in
.I matches
(at most 100 lines).
The caller must free each line and then the array itself.
.SH RETURN VALUE
The number of matching lines, or \-1 on failure.
